{"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidentalmark\/value"]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"value","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"value"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"MXLAccidentalValue","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLAccidentalValueO","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLAccidentalMarkV5valueAA0C5ValueOvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalMark"]]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"value"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLAccidentalValue","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLAccidentalValueO"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalMark\/value"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The value of this element."}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAccidentalMark/value":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"value","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"value"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLAccidentalValue","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLAccidentalValueO"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidentalmark\/value","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The value of this element."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalMark\/value"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAccidentalMark":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An accidental-mark can be used as a separate notation or as part of an ornament. When used in an ornament,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position and placement are relative to the ornament, not relative to the note."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidentalmark","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAccidentalMark"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLAccidentalMark","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAccidentalMark"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalMark","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAccidentalValue":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The accidental-value type represents notated accidentals supported by MusicXML. In the MusicXML 2.0 DTD this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"was a string with values that could be included. The XSD strengthens the data typing to an enumerated list."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The quarter- and three-quarters- accidentals are Tartini-style quarter-tone accidentals. The -down and -up"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidentals are quarter-tone accidentals that include arrows pointing down or up. The slash- accidentals are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used in Turkish classical music. The numbered sharp and flat accidentals are superscripted versions of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidental signs, used in Turkish folk music. The sori and koron accidentals are microtonal sharp and flat"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidentals used in Iranian and Persian music. The other accidental covers accidentals other than those listed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"here. It is usually used in combination with the smufl attribute to specify a particular SMuFL accidental. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smufl attribute may be used with any accidental value to help specify the appearance of symbols that share the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same MusicXML semantics."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidentalvalue","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAccidentalValue"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLAccidentalValue","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAccidentalValue"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue","role":"symbol"}}}